data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"For one request with arrival `a` and token times `t[0] < ... < t[n-1]`: TTFT is `t[0] - a`, end-to-end is\n`t[n-1] - a`, and mean ITL is `(t[n-1] - t[0]) / (n - 1)` when `n >= 2`. Percentiles use linear interpolation: with\n`m` sorted values, the position is `h = (m - 1) * p / 100`. Take the values on either side of `h` and weight them by\nthe fractional part of `h`. Do not round `h` to the nearest rank."},"hints_note":null}

